              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for childhood, then the Latin for to bring up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: bulla, bullae",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bulla, bullae — \"an amulet (worn by a child); a bubble\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Puer bullam auream in collō gerēbat. The boy wore a golden amulet round his neck."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. First a bubble, then the round locket a freeborn boy wore until he came of age. English bullet and the papal bull come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bulla first meant \"a bubble\", anything swelling into a round shape (Lewis & Short); where the word comes from is not settled. English bull, a papal letter with a round seal, comes from it, and bullet through French."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
